{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 210 "" 0 "" {TEXT 208 21 "Review Questions - 06"
 }{TEXT 213 0 "" }{TEXT 208 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 214 6 "Note: " }{TEXT 215 201 "Please answer the
 following questions to review Lecture 6. You may need to try some Map
le commands and answer the review questions under the help of your lec
ture notes and the Maple built-in help menu." }}{PARA 211 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 208 2 "  " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 60 "1. What is th
e output of the following sequence of commands?" }}{PARA 208 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 227 16 ">(x, y):=(1,2):\n" }{TEXT 227 13 "  f:=proc(n)\n" }{TEXT
 227 16 "       local x;\n" }{TEXT 227 17 "       global y;\n" }{TEXT 
227 14 "       x:=20;\n" }{TEXT 227 13 "       y:=5;\n" }{TEXT 227 21 
"       return n*x*y;\n" }{TEXT 227 13 "   end proc:\n" }{TEXT 227 15 
"   f(2), x, y;\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 208 10 "Solution: "
 }{TEXT 216 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 14 "(x,y):=(
1,2):\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "f:=proc(n)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "  local x;
\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 12 "  global y;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "  x:=20;\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "  y:=5;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 16 "  return n*x*y;\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "end proc:\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "f(2), x, y;" }}{PARA 
11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6%\"$+#\"\"\"\"\"&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 208 173 "The output is the product of 2, 20 and 5. The proc char
ges the value of y outside of the proc while the value of x only chang
es within the proc. This is why x=1 and y=5 now." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 33 "2. How to view Ma
ple source code?" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "
" 0 "" {TEXT 208 10 "Solution: " }{TEXT 217 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 
0 "" {TEXT 208 66 "The command showstat will allow you to view the Map
le source code." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}{PARA 0 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 226 142 "3. Write a procedure that takes an indeterminate \+
number of numbers and returns the floating point average of the number
s using args and nargs." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 208 10 "Solution: " }{TEXT 218 0 "" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 12 "Avg:=proc()\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 13 "  \+
local i,A;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 21 "  if nargs = 0 then \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 
46 "    error \"there are no numbers to average\"; \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 
10 "  end if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 30 "  A:=add(args[i],i=1..nargs);\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 25 "  return evalf(A/nargs);\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "end proc
:" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 34 "Avg
(10.8,2,3,3,4,5); Avg(2,4,6,8);" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 ""
 {XPPMATH 20 "$\"+LLLLY!\"*" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "$\"\"&\"
\"!" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
226 67 "4. What is the command to compute the n-th iterate of a functi
on f?" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 208 10 "Solution: " }{TEXT 219 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 45 "(f@@n)(x);truef:=x->2*x mod 5; (truef@@5)(6);" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "--I#@@G6$%*protectedGI(_syslibG6\"6$I\"f
GF(I\"nGF(6#\"\"\"" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I&truefG6\"f*6#I
\"xGF$F$6$I)operatorGF$I&arrowGF$F$-I$modGF$6$,$*&\"\"#\"\"\"F'F1F1\"
\"&F$F$F$" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 101 "5. What is the o
ption which causes Maple to print out more details about the behavior \+
of a procedure?" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 208 10 "Solution: " }{TEXT 220 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> "
 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 80 "6. Write a recursive procedure to comput
e n!  Note that 0! = 1 and n! = n*(n-1)!" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 226 
0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 208 10 "Solution: " }{TEXT 221 0 
"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 16 "myfact:=proc(n)\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 52 "if n=0 then return 1; else n*procname(n-1); end if;\n
" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "end proc:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 
0 21 "myfact(0); myfact(3);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"\"" }
}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
